---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Nations · Meridian"
  description="Every nation on Meridian, ranked by the Meridian Development Index, and the land atlas behind it. Rebuilt from live server data."
  path="/nations"
  analytics
>
<main class="doc">
  <h1>Nations</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every nation on Meridian, ranked by the Meridian Development Index, rebuilt from the land databases. For how claiming, upkeep, and nations actually work, see the <a href="/lands">Lands guide</a>.</p>
  <div class="data-stale" data-stale hidden></div>

  <section class="analytics" data-analytics>
    <div class="nation-grid" data-slot="nation-grid"></div>

    <h2>Land atlas</h2>
    <div data-slot="land-table"></div>

    <details class="method">
      <summary>How the Meridian Development Index is calculated</summary>
      <div class="m-body">
        <p>The MDI is a single score from <code>0</code> to <code>1</code>, modelled on the way the UN builds its Human Development Index: measure a few things that matter, put each on the same scale, then combine them so a nation cannot coast on one strength alone.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Territory</dt><dd>Claimed chunks, against a reference ceiling of 60.</dd>
          <dt>Population</dt><dd>Trusted members across the nation's lands, against a ceiling of 15.</dd>
          <dt>Wealth</dt><dd>Combined land-bank treasury, against a ceiling of $5,000,000.</dd>
          <dt>Activity</dt><dd>Recent presence and events in the nation's lands.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>The four sub-indices are combined with a <strong>geometric mean</strong>, so a nation that is large but empty, or rich but tiny, scores lower than one that is balanced. Reference ceilings are tuned as the server grows.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
